  "nonogramTutorialWelcomeTitle": "Welcome to Nonopix!",
  "nonogramTutorialWelcome": "Let's learn the basic rules with a small 5×5 puzzle.",
  "nonogramTutorialStart": "Start",
  "nonogramTutorialSwitchToFill": "Puzzles are solved by filling in squares. Tap the button below to switch to fill mode.",
  "nonogramTutorialClueIsCount": "The number tells you how many squares in the row are filled. This row has 5, so fill them all!",
  "nonogramTutorialEdgeCell": "The last square is already filled. The block of 4 must include it, so there is only one way to place it: fill the 3 squares to its left.",
  "nonogramTutorialMultipleClues": "More than one number means more than one block, with at least one empty square between them. 2 2 fits these 5 squares in only one way.",
  "nonogramTutorialClueOrder": "Order matters too: 3 1 means the block of 3 comes first, then the block of 1.",
  "nonogramTutorialColumns": "Columns have numbers too, read from top to bottom. Switch to X mode to mark squares that must stay empty.",
  "nonogramTutorialMarkEmpty": "Columns with a ✓ already have all their squares. Mark their remaining empty squares with an X.",
  "nonogramTutorialOneCellLeft": "The 1 in the last row now has only one place left. Switch back to fill mode.",
  "nonogramTutorialFinish": "Fill the last square to finish the puzzle!",
  "nonogramTutorialDoneTitle": "Well done!",
  "nonogramTutorialDone": "You're all set! On big puzzles, drag with two fingers (or from the empty space outside the grid) to move the board; the app will remind you on your first big puzzle.",
